{"title":"2002 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 22","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A set of tiles numbered 1 through 100 is modified repeatedly by the following operation: remove all tiles numbered with a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Perfect_square\" title=\"Perfect square\">perfect square</a>, and renumber the remaining tiles consecutively starting with 1. How many times must the operation be performed to reduce the number of tiles in the set to one?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/4/bf4da4caa41a981cf84d5b220a56f56fb5cb62a4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(A)}\\ 10 \\qquad \\text{(B)}\\ 11 \\qquad \\text{(C)}\\ 18 \\qquad \\text{(D)}\\ 19 \\qquad \\text{(E)}\\ 20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"375\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The pattern is quite simple to see after listing a couple of terms.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/a/efafb217eec4c75df3fa82aa8da5e175c238050d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\begin{tabular}{|r|r|r|} \\hline \\#&amp;\\text{Removed}&amp;\\text{Left}\\\\ \\hline 1&amp;10&amp;90\\\\ 2&amp;9&amp;81\\\\ 3&amp;9&amp;72\\\\ 4&amp;8&amp;64\\\\ 5&amp;8&amp;56\\\\ 6&amp;7&amp;49\\\\ 7&amp;7&amp;42\\\\ 8&amp;6&amp;36\\\\ 9&amp;6&amp;30\\\\ 10&amp;5&amp;25\\\\ 11&amp;5&amp;20\\\\ 12&amp;4&amp;16\\\\ 13&amp;4&amp;12\\\\ 14&amp;3&amp;9\\\\ 15&amp;3&amp;6\\\\ 16&amp;2&amp;4\\\\ 17&amp;2&amp;2\\\\ 18&amp;1&amp;1\\\\     \\hline \\end{tabular}\\]\" width=\"173\" height=\"381\" />\n</p><p>Thus, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/7/1f731aad5c1cdc3c3b70667b3e1285045107cab2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\text{(C) } 18}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"60\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Given <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/0/6006bba637eef443381fbaff768fa62d9ff41e62.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"17\" /> tiles, a step removes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> tiles, leaving <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/5/0a5dcc157a1564c55ef9cb3c70f05b8473bf1a09.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n^2 - n$\" width=\"51\" height=\"15\" /> tiles behind. Now, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/e/c0ee08b0432bf992cd453e23ca55276b626b6a36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(n-1)^2 = n^2 - n + (1-n) &lt; n^2 - n &lt; n^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"335\" height=\"19\" />, so in the next step <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/d/4bdca93962a2beaffc172ca394e04fe05bd74ffd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"15\" /> tiles are removed. This gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/1/aa173ed67884b1744df1fea61ab1be271f51a1ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(n^2 - n) - (n-1) = n^2 - 2n + 1 = (n-1)^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"350\" height=\"21\" />, another perfect square.\n</p><p>Thus each two steps we cycle down a perfect square, and in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/7/177bc2ae20bc3e3c012b07e02584b35e319812e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(10-1)\\times 2 = 18$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"136\" height=\"18\" /> steps, we are left with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> tile, hence our answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/7/1f731aad5c1cdc3c3b70667b3e1285045107cab2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\text{(C) } 18}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"60\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We start of with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/0/f40cfedafdfb7cb45d387ecd791625b9fa4e59bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100 = 10 \\cdot 10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"103\" height=\"14\" /> numbers. When we use the certain operation, call if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/f/6efaaf74e576202fad965134bc49c6a34aac4c30.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"41\" height=\"20\" />, have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/0/0403025fcde65af166b5586956d0573bcf11d8d0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100 - 10 = 90 = 10 \\cdot 9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"177\" height=\"15\" />.\nThen we do <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/f/6efaaf74e576202fad965134bc49c6a34aac4c30.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"41\" height=\"20\" /> again, to subtract <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> numbers and get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/f/5ef25c1522f227d2eb2ba078d02617ec87e51455.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9 \\cdot 9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"33\" height=\"14\" />. In the end, we will want <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/b/0fbe03d83c16d57bb2c4a714f6d087313df54ef5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 = 1 \\cdot 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"66\" height=\"14\" />. We can say we have to use <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/f/6efaaf74e576202fad965134bc49c6a34aac4c30.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"41\" height=\"20\" /> once to make <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/4/a246689b11802fc59fe14fb2239d7cfd82e73ea6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\cdot n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"37\" height=\"10\" /> into <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/4/194f3cedb2c064ad84f7815da7f28ac24a493275.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\cdot (n-1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"82\" height=\"20\" />. Thus we must use it twice to get from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/4/a246689b11802fc59fe14fb2239d7cfd82e73ea6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\cdot n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"37\" height=\"10\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/4/b54dbf5b95512a72d87d61028793c093b3c70150.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(n-1)(n-1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"115\" height=\"20\" />. For example, it takes us <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/f/6efaaf74e576202fad965134bc49c6a34aac4c30.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"41\" height=\"20\" /> to get from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/8/4b868bf3ef9b5d60b9a2077011e23cd1420cef24.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10 \\cdot 10$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"49\" height=\"13\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/f/5ef25c1522f227d2eb2ba078d02617ec87e51455.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9 \\cdot 9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"33\" height=\"14\" />. Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/f/6efaaf74e576202fad965134bc49c6a34aac4c30.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"41\" height=\"20\" /> to get from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/f/5ef25c1522f227d2eb2ba078d02617ec87e51455.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9 \\cdot 9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"33\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/1/dc16eaf3fecd0d771369171dd397a42a2880a391.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8 \\cdot 8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"33\" height=\"14\" />. You should try this with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, and see it works. This means we can have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> be the number we start with, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> be the number we want. Then we would use <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/f/6efaaf74e576202fad965134bc49c6a34aac4c30.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"41\" height=\"20\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/c/87c33c9c6c6d0b9fcd21d6199d882f3811266a1a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2(n - 1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"67\" height=\"20\" /> times to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/c/92c5770c5ac85900b35548289121eda8fbab3ad0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 \\cdot 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"33\" height=\"14\" />. Substituting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/2/2428d7e6aacea81218b944240125f5308854cdd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2(10-1) = 2 \\cdot 9 = \\boxed{18}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"184\" height=\"25\" />.\n- Wiselion\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=CuKko0JpIdQ\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=CuKko0JpIdQ</a>   ~David\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10A\" title=\"2002 AMC 10A\">2002 AMC 10A</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10A_Problems\" title=\"2002 AMC 10A Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10A_Answer_Key\" title=\"2002 AMC 10A Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_21\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2002 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 21\">Problem 21</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"2002 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 23\">Problem 23</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2002 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2002 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_3\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2002 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_4\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2002 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_5\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2002 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_6\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2002 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_7\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2002 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_8\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2002 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2002 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_10\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2002 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_11\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2002 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_12\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2002 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2002 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_14\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2002 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2002 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 15\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"2002 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 16\">16</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_17\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2002 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 17\">17</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"2002 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 18\">18</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"2002 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 19\">19</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"2002 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 20\">20</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_21\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2002 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 21\">21</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">22</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"2002 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 23\">23</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_24\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2002 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 24\">24</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_25\" title=\"2002 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 25\">25</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AMC_10_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AMC 10 Problems and Solutions\"> All AMC 10 Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261016210610\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.038 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.059 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 315/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 2324/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 158/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 8013/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   13.178      1 -total\n 60.43%    7.964      1 Template:AMC10_box\n 38.62%    5.089      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:6405:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261016210610 and revision id 198183. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}